The '''Warthogs''' were a [[Sentience|sentient]] [[species]]. They were notable for their long snouts and [[Tooth|tusks]]. One [[Unidentified Warthog pirate|Warthog]] served as a [[pirate]] for [[Captain]] [[Gorian Shard]] onboard [[Gorian Shard's pirate Corsair|his corsair]]<ref name="Chapter 17" /> while another [[Unidentified Warthog alien|Warthog pirate]] was a member of [[Silvo's pirates]].<ref name="SC 101">{{SkeletonCrew|This Could Be a Real Adventure}}</ref>

{{Species-stub}}

==Behind the scenes==
The Warthog species first appeared in the [[Chapter 17: The Apostate|first episode]] of the [[The Mandalorian Season Three|third season]] of ''[[Star Wars: The Mandalorian]]''. The species was identified in the credits for the episode.<ref name="Chapter 17" /> In the real world [[wikipedia:Warthog|Warthogs (''Phacochoerus'')]] are a genus of [[Wikipedia:Suidae|pig]] with a similar looking head, native to sub-Saharan Africa.

